      "extract": "In the application of random matrices we have learned to appreciate the predictive power for spectral correlations, depending on the location within the spectrum. One example is the micro- scopic Bessel-density close to the origin, that is relevant when chiral symmetry is important, e.g. in comparison to data from lattice QCD. It depends heavily on the number of zero-modes ν, that characterise different topological",
